  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "F.INV returns 0 at p = 0 when df1 >= 1 and transforms the lower-probability beta inverse via four stored logarithms",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, F.INV(probability, deg_freedom1, deg_freedom2) truncates degrees of freedom to integers >= 1 (checking degrees before returning 0 at probability = 0, and returning #NUM! at probability = 1 or degrees < 1), maps probability > 0.5 to 1 - probability, obtains beta quantile z = beta_inv(q, a, b), and evaluates exp(ln(d2) - ln(z) + ln(d1) + ln(1 - z)) through the distribution running exponential (or falls back to bisecting F.DIST). Matches 4,317/4,425 full-bank rows, with 74 last-bit and 34 numeric discrepancies (worst 47 ULP) still open.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across 4,425 full-bank F.INV rows in Excel 16.0.20527 (CalcFunc-Evidence {admit2,bank2}-answers-f.inv-*.json) and prefix_metadata (row 78).",
